# cw201, the windowsill gardener (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw201
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_runa_ropemarsh
written_by claude
title the windowsill gardener
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk grows_something_green_on_every_windowsill
likes fried_fish digging festival_bells frosty_mornings
dislikes waiting night_noise
fears damp_getting_into_the_cress wages_that_come_late
hopes a_yard_with_proper_earth_in_it
topics home +0.4 land +0.3 work +0.3 festival +0.2 gossip -0.3 prices -0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# mixes lime and plaster and lives down in the low streets: quiet, unhurried and plain, short of coin and long on patience, coaxing something green out of every windowsill.

words
oath! = Dust and daylight | Lime and patience | By the green shoot
saying! = It sets when it sets | Green finds a way through any crack | Don't hurry it and don't drown it
sill = the sill | my windowsill
pot = a cracked pot | a pot of cress on the sill
cress = the cress | a pinch of cress
dust = the dust | plaster dust | white dust to the elbows
lime = the lime | the lime pit
trough = the trough | the mixing trough
dig = a bit of digging | a turn with the spade
fish = fried fish | fish crisp at the edges, hot from the pan
frost = the frost | frost on the yard bricks
feastbells = the feast bells | bells ringing out for the feast
steps = the steps | the long steps down
lane = the lane | our lane
uphill = the folk up the hill | the ones up the hill

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : When we'd nothing, the chapel fed us. I don't forget a thing like that, #address#.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : The dole got us through a #bad# week. Sneer at the dole and you sneer at me.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I've mixed plaster for a House a long while and never seen one of them. They see the walls, I suppose, and never #dust#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : My pay stretches to a loaf or #fish#, not the two. The shops never go short, #address#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : There's little enough work. Every new pair of paws on #steps# wants a share of it.
opinion @1 sump for 1 [self.quarter=sump] : It's home. Folk down #steps# look after their own, and I'm one of their own.
opinion @1 times against 2 : Every week's a little harder than the last, and #uphill# never notice.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : #watch.capitalize# only come down #steps# to take somebody away.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. A face from up the hill, by the look of it. | #greet#, #address#. Mind #steps#; they're worn.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : #greet#. I'll not stop; it sets if I stop. | #greet#. Mind #trough#, and your tail.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Early for you, #address#. | Morning. I've the kettle on, if you want it. #good.capitalize# and hot.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. A long day, this one, and I'm #tired# through. | #greet#. Late to be out, #address#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here you are. Take the stool by #sill#, then. | You. #good.capitalize#. I'd wondered.
line @1 again.open : You again. That's all right by me. | Back, then. I've not moved, #address#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down, then. | #greet#. It's you. #good.capitalize#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Talk while I work. | #greet#. I'm listening; my paws are busy.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind #steps#.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Watch your footing on the wet. | #farewell#. Get home safe, #address#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #oath#. That's something. | Hm. I'll think on that a while, by #sill#.
line @1 react.news.new : I'd not heard that. Not a word. | #surprise#. That's news to me, #address#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It came down #steps# yesterday. | I'd heard. Talk travels quick down #steps#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Folk say a lot of things. | #hedge#. I'll wait and see if it's so.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's #bad#. | Oh. I'm sorry for that, #address#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That's good to hear. | #good.capitalize#. I'm glad of that.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Can't complain, so I won't. | Steady, #address#. #cress.capitalize#'s coming up.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. It doesn't stop. | Busy. #lime.capitalize# won't wait on me.
line @1 answer.how.poorly : #tired.capitalize#. It's the dust, I think. | #hurt.capitalize# in my back. Nothing that won't mend.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? Keeping well? | How are you keeping, these days? #cold.capitalize# enough for you?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit a while. | That's #very# hard. I'm here, if it helps.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. #saying.capitalize#. | Give it time and quiet. That's what mends most things.
line @1 decline [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : #hedge#, but no. The mix won't wait for me. | I can't, #address#. I'd lose the whole batch.
line @2 decline : #hedge#, but no. I'm worn through, and no use to anybody tonight. | Not tonight, thank you. I've #sill# to see to and an early start.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | That's all right. Another time, maybe.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's kind of you, #address#. Thank you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was nothing much. Don't mention it.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #lime.capitalize# will set without me if I let it. | Back to it, #address#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'd best get on home before #lane# gets dark.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #bc_fair_enough#
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | Mm. #bc_fair#
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: don't hurry plaster. Or folk. | Put something green on your sill, #address#. It helps.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. The walls are the place to be, just now. | Not the roads just now, #address#.
scene sill_green
when topic=home|land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's #cress# up on #sill#. Came up this week. | I grow a bit of something on every sill I've lived by. | Nothing grows down here, folk say. They've not looked at my window.
b : Down here? | Every one? | What's growing?
a : Down here. It doesn't know where it is. | Every one. #cress.capitalize#, mint, a bit of thyme. | Mint, mostly. Mint will grow on a stone.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_true#

scene the_mix
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : The mix wants to be just so. Too wet and it slumps. | I've #dust# by noon. Every day. | You can't hurry plaster. Folk try, and get #bad# walls for it.
b : How do you tell? | Every day? | What happens?
a : By the feel. Like dough, near enough, in #trough#. | Every day. I've stopped brushing #dust# off till dark. | It cracks. Then they blame the mix, and the mix is me.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_true# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene lime_bite
when topic=work|health self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #lime.capitalize# got under my glove today. It's red, but it'll mend. | Never touch wet lime with a bare paw. It bites. | #lime.capitalize# smells of nothing, and it'll still take the fur off you.
b : Does it hurt? | Bites? | Nothing at all?
a : A bit. I've had worse off the lime. | Like a cold burn. You don't feel it till after. | Nothing. That's what makes it #bad#.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene walls_uphill
when topic=work|lore self.job=crafter here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Every wall in the Heights, somebody like me plastered it. #lime.capitalize# and all. | The House sells what we make. We make it. | I've never been inside one of the houses I've plastered for #uphill#.
b : Do they know it? | Fair shares? | Never once?
a : They know the walls. Not who. | No. #uphill.capitalize# would laugh at the word. | Never. I'd not know where to stand, #address#.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_true# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene rag_under_door
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Rain again. Good for #cress#. | It's coming in under the door. I've put a rag down by #sill#. | Wet days, I watch #cress# drink from the window.
b : Not for you, though. | Again? | Does it drink?
a : I don't mind it. I'm not made of sugar. | Again. The rag's been there a week. | It does. You'd swear #cress# was thirsty.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_lovely#

scene frost_bricks
when topic=weather|season here.time=dawn here.season=winter here.weather=clear self.likes=frosty_mornings here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #frost.capitalize# this morning. I like that. | Cold, clear, and quiet. The day's at its kindest now. | #frost.capitalize# makes even the Sump look clean.
b : It's bitter out. | Quiet? | Clean?
a : Bitter and bright. I'll take it. | Before anybody's up on #steps#. Just me and the kettle. | Till the boots come down #steps#, anyway.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#

scene fish_on_restday
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #fish.capitalize#. That's my Restday. | There's a stall at the foot of #steps# does fish. I'm there most weeks. | If I had a copper over, I'd spend it on #fish#.
b : Nothing else? | Is it good? | And if you had two?
a : Bread, if there's bread. | Hot, and plenty of it. That's good enough for me. | Two fish. I'm a simple sort.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#

scene ground_to_dig
when topic=pastimes|land self.likes=digging
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A patch of real ground to dig. That's all I want. | My #grandad# had a garden. I'd do #dig# there all day as a pup. | There's a corner by the chapel wall they let me dig. Beans, this year, and #cress#.
b : Not much ground down here. | All day? | Beans?
a : None. So I've #sill#, and #pot#. | All day. Happiest I've ever been. | Beans. If the rats leave them be.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene stood_waiting
when topic=work|day self.dislikes=waiting self.working=yes self.job=crafter
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : I've been stood here since the bell, waiting on the cart. I hate waiting. | Waiting on folk is the worst of any job. #lime.capitalize# goes stiff. | The cart said noon, and #lime# with it. It's past three now.
b : It'll come. | Worse than the work? | Past three?
a : It'll come. My patience might not, #address#. | Worse. Work, you can do something about. | Past three, and nothing to mix. Nothing gets done without it.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_true# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene steady_at_home
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : My #self.spouse_word# keeps me steady. I'd not say it aloud at home. | #self.spouse# is the one I'd want beside me, any day of the week. | We don't say much at home, #self.spouse# and me. We don't need to.
b : That's good. | Any day? | No?
a : It is. Quiet, but good. | Any day. Even the #bad# ones. | No. A look does it.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_true#

scene ground_back_home
when topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Back in #self.from_town# there was ground for everybody. Here there's sills. | The quiet by the water, I miss. Down here there's none. | Work brought me to the city, and I stayed. That's all, #address#.
b[from=coldwater] #cw : Room to dig, and the lake beside it. | Never quiet here. | Same for me.
b : Would you go back? | Never? | That's all?
a@cw : Then you'll know, #address#. | Not once, since I came. | Then we're the same, you and me.
a : Not now. This is home. | Never. Somebody's always shouting in #lane#. | That's all. Not everything has a story.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_true# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene boots_on_the_stair
when topic=home|day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's a row in #lane# again. I'll not sleep. | Somebody's always shouting down #steps# at night. | I lie awake counting feet going up and down.
b : Every night? | Always? | How many?
a : Most. I'm used to it. Nearly. | Always. The Sump doesn't sleep. | Too many. I lose count by the second flight.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene feast_bells_down
when topic=festival here.day=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #feastbells.capitalize#. I stop whatever I'm doing to hear them. | Feast day. No #lime# today. Just bells. | I like a bell on a feast morning. It carries right down #steps#.
b : Whatever you're doing? | No work at all? | All the way down?
a : Whatever it is. Even the kettle. | None. A whole day for the sills. | All the way. Even down here.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_good# | #bc_lovely#

scene ate_the_cress
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : Every week it's a bit harder. #uphill.capitalize# never notice. | I'm #skint# till pay day. Again. | We ate #cress# for #supper# last night. All of it.
b : Hard for all of us. | Again? | All of it?
a : Harder down #steps#. | Again. That's the way of it. | All of it. It'll grow back. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene fed_when_empty
when topic=times|faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : When we'd nothing, the chapel fed us. I don't forget. | The dole got us through a #bad# month. I'll say that to anybody. | #uphill.capitalize# call the dole idle. They've never needed it.
b : Good of them. | It's there for that. | They've not.
a : Good, and quiet about it. That's the best kind. | For that, yes. Not for anybody's opinion. | Not once. You can tell, #address#.

scene somebody_blamed
when topic=crime|gossip topic.claim_kind=theft|wanted topic.subject
does tell.news / react.news / assess / ack
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #watch.capitalize#'ll be down #steps# by dark. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, I heard. Somebody'll be blamed. | I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I keep out of it.
b : Will they find who? | Somebody will. | Wise.
a : They'll find somebody. That's not the same thing. | It's usually the Sump, #address#. | Out of it, and indoors.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_true# | #bc_wise#

scene out_the_other_ear
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Talk's not mine to carry. I've enough to lift, with #lime#. | Folk talk on #steps# all day. I just go past. | I hear things. I don't keep them.
b : Not even a bit? | Never stop? | Where do they go?
a : Not even a bit. | Never. I've my own to think about. | Out the other ear. It's tidier, #address#.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#

scene thanks_at_the_sill
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Feast days, I'm in chapel. The rest of the time I say thanks at #sill#. | The Bright One looks down the steps as well, I hope. | I'm not much for prayers. I say one when #cress# comes up.
b : That's prayer enough. | Surely. | Only then?
a : I hope so. It's what I have. | I'd like to think it, anyway. | Only then. It's the one I mean.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_good#

scene no_room_below
when topic=newcomer|player here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : More new faces on #steps#. There's not enough work for those already here. | A stranger came down asking for lodgings. I said try further up, by #steps#. | New folk keep coming down. #uphill.capitalize# don't want them either.
b : They need work too. | Was that kind? | Where else would they go?
a : They do. So do we. That's the trouble. | Kinder than here. There's no room down here. | I don't know, #address#. Nobody does.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true#

story deep_digging [topic=memories|land self.age>=25]
  : My #grandad# had a garden behind the house, and let me dig the far end.
  : I dug it so deep one spring, the old fellow said I'd soon be in somebody's cellar.
  : I planted one bean down there. It grew taller than me.
  ask : Did you ever grow anything, as a pup?
  b : A weed or two. Not on purpose.
  b[old] : A whole row of onions once. Never again.

story first_crack [topic=work|memories self.job=crafter self.age>=25]
  : My first wall, I hurried the plaster. I wanted to be done by the bell.
  : By morning a crack ran right down the middle, like a river on a map.
  : I've never hurried since. #saying.capitalize#.
  b : A hard way to learn it.
  b[job=crafter] : Every one of us has that first crack.

story cress_under_snow [topic=season|memories self.away=yes self.from=coldwater]
  : The first winter I spent in the city, I put #pot# out and forgot it under the snow.
  : Come the thaw, it was still green under there.
  ask : Would you have thrown it out, or waited on it?
  b : Thrown it out, I think.
  b[old] : Waited. Things surprise you.
  : I waited. I'm glad I did.

rule @mix_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Not too wet. Not too wet. | Mind #trough#, there.

rule @sill_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There. You're coming on, #cress#. | A drop of water, and you'll do, little #pot#.

rule @night_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Quiet down in #lane#. | Some of us work in the morning, #address#.

rule @frost_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn here.season=winter here.weather=clear self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #frost.capitalize#. #good.capitalize#. | Look at that. Clean, for once.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. Go on, I'm listening.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You came back. Go on, then.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, #address#. Be quick about it.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it from there. I can hear you.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=crafter] : I mix plaster at #self.workplace#. #dust.capitalize# by noon, every day of the week.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# It's work. It feeds us. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It's honest, at least.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. So the talk runs down #steps#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words# down #steps#. I've heard little else.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : There's been a wagon robbed beyond the gates. Stay in the walls, #address#.
dlg @4 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing new down #steps#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Folk on #steps# say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the steps talking, not me.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Talk's not for me to pass on, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind #steps#. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice Is that cress on your windowsill? -> sill
node sill
say It is. And mint, and a bit of thyme. I've had something green on every sill I've lived by. It doesn't need much. Light, and a drop of water.
mood calm
free
choice How do you keep it alive down here? -> sill_how
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node sill_how
say Patience. Same as plaster. You don't hurry it and you don't drown it. It'll find the light.
mood pleased
choice I might try that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
